Using S50_ARTIFACT_AND_IO, S60_EVALUATION_QC, and S20_HYDRA_CONFIG to keep export artifacts/manifest consistent, add split stats, and wire Hydra configs cleanly.

Implemented `process=export` to package generate artifacts into deterministic train/val/test splits with a fixed dataset_id, and produced index tables plus manifest/metrics/splits for downstream training use. The core logic lives in `src/synthlab/processes/export.py`, which resolves input artifacts, computes split assignments from the root seed, writes parquet/csv data + sample/particle indexes, and records dataset_id plus split summaries in `manifest.json`, `metrics/export_summary.json`, and `splits/splits.json`. Hydra defaults are added in `conf/process/export.yaml` and `conf/wafer_particles/export/default.yaml`, and smoke coverage is added in `tests/test_process_smoke.py` (uses CSV output to avoid pyarrow dependency).

